    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d561">

                <pb facs="0769" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.9411/24: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi><anchor
                        n="86" xml:id="d561-f1"/></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1920-03-25T12:30:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1920-03-20T00:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>].<lb/>[Received March 25, 1920—12:30
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>65. A report has been received from the Chinese Minister in Great Britain that
                    the Japanese envoys are negotiating with the British for a renewal of the
                    Anglo–Japanese Alliance. It is my hope that the Alliance will not be renewed as
                    that would have an unfortunate effect in China.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d561-f1" n="86" type="source" xml:id="d561-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated by the Secretary of State to Great Britain as no. 314, Mar. 26, 4
                    p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
